course: dictionary
lesson: 5949
title: Mastermind: the clever planner
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mastermind is a very clever person who plans something difficult. As a verb, to mastermind means to plan and organise something difficult and clever. In the story, «Badger's was the mastermind» means Badger was the one who thought up the plan.
explain: The words around it give you clues. Toad says the Mole and the Water Rat «bore the brunt of the fighting», so they took the hardest part. Toad says he «served in the ranks», which means he was an ordinary soldier, not the planner. So a mastermind is the person who thinks up the plan, not the person who does most of the fighting.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Badger's was the thinking-up of the plan» still makes sense, so mastermind fits. Notice that the word can be a noun (a mastermind) or a verb (to mastermind).
fact: A mastermind is a very clever person who plans something difficult.
fact: «Mastermind» can also be a verb: to plan and organise something difficult and clever.
fact: «Bore the brunt» means took the hardest part.
fact: «Served in the ranks» means was an ordinary soldier, not a leader.
fact: In the UK, Mastermind is a famous TV quiz show with a black chair.
exercise: Toad says Badger «was the mastermind». What does mastermind mean here? | The one who cooked the food | The one who sang the songs | *The one who planned the clever plan | The one who did the most fighting
exercise: «The Mole and the Water Rat bore the brunt of the fighting.» What does bore the brunt mean? | They watched from a tree | They sang to cheer everyone up | They ran away early | *They took the hardest part
exercise: Which sentence uses mastermind as a verb, an action word? | The mastermind sat in the black chair | Badger is a clever mastermind | Badger has a big mastermind | *Badger will mastermind the plan to win back Toad Hall
test: «Toad said he served in the ranks.» What does served in the ranks mean? | He was the cook in the castle | He was the captain of the whole army | *He was an ordinary soldier, not the leader | He was Badger's best friend
test: Which word means a very clever person who plans something difficult? | Parade | *Mastermind | Brunt | Murmur
exam: Which best describes a mastermind? | A person who is always late for school | *A person who thinks up a clever, difficult plan | A person who only does the hardest fighting | A person who sings loudly at parties
